%% KYNZA — Supabase Realtime Subscription Lifecycle (verified 2026-07-03)
%% Actual pattern: NOT a hand-rolled RealtimeChannel/.channel() service — every
%% consumer uses the supabase_flutter SDK's high-level query builder:
%% SupabaseService.client.from(table).stream(primaryKey: ['id']).eq(column, value)
%% Confirmed real consumers (grep across lib/): bookings (by client_id, salon_id,
%% practitioner_id), payment_screen (single booking by id), proxipay_qr_screen
%% (transactions by booking_id) & proxipay session (by id), services (by salon_id),
%% staff_profiles (by salon_id), loyalty_cards (by client_id), marketing contacts
%% + promotions (by salon_id), notification_logs (by user_id) x2, journey (by salon_id).
%% Enabled at DB level via 20260624040000_enable_realtime_publication.sql.
sequenceDiagram
    participant Screen as Screen/Provider (per role)
    participant SDK as supabase_flutter SDK
    participant WS as Realtime WebSocket
    participant PG as Postgres (logical replication)

    Screen->>SDK: client.from('bookings').stream(primaryKey:['id']).eq('salon_id', id)
    SDK->>WS: open WS connection, subscribe to postgres_changes\nfiltered server-side by salon_id/client_id/user_id
    WS->>PG: attach to supabase_realtime publication
    PG-->>WS: initial snapshot (first .listen() emission)
    WS-->>SDK: row set
    SDK-->>Screen: List<Model> via .map()

    Note over PG,WS: any INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on the filtered table

    PG-->>WS: change event
    WS-->>SDK: pushed row diff
    SDK-->>Screen: new List<Model> emission (screen rebuilds)

    Note over Screen,WS: Reconnection — handled internally by the SDK's\nRealtimeClient (auto-retry with backoff), no app-level\nreconnect/backoff code exists in lib/ today — this is\nSDK-default behavior, not a KYNZA-authored strategy.

    WS--xSDK: connection dropped (network loss)
    SDK->>SDK: internal reconnect attempt (SDK default backoff)
    SDK->>WS: re-subscribe on reconnect
    WS-->>SDK: resync snapshot

    rect rgb(40,30,0)
    Note over Screen: Per-role scoping is achieved purely by the .eq() filter\nvalue (salon_id for owner/manager/staff feeds, client_id\nfor client feeds, user_id for notifications) — there is no\nseparate "channel per role" concept in the codebase.
    end
